🧠 Neural Regulation of Complex Traits
Research Question
How do neural systems regulate complex biological traits and behaviours, and what genomic mechanisms support these processes?

🌊 Background
Complex traits such as behaviour, sensory perception, decision-making, communication, and environmental responses are controlled by neural systems interacting with genetic and molecular pathways. Understanding how neural activity translates into observable biological traits is a major challenge in modern biology.
Advances in neuroscience, genomics, and bioinformatics have made it possible to investigate how genes, neural circuits, and environmental factors interact to shape complex phenotypes. Marine organisms provide unique opportunities to study these questions because many possess highly specialized nervous systems, sensory adaptations, and behaviours that have evolved in response to diverse environmental pressures.
This project explores how neural regulation influences complex traits and how genomic approaches can be used to investigate these processes.


